---
const currentYear = new Date().getFullYear();

import "../style.css";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    />

    <title>Viktoriia Matviieva | WordPress Developer Portfolio</title>

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="WordPress developer portfolio featuring custom themes, Elementor websites, ACF, Custom Post Types, responsive development, SEO, and website performance work."
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="portfolio-page">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero__content">
          <p class="hero__eyebrow">WordPress Developer Portfolio</p>

          <h1 class="hero__title">
            Hi, I’m Viktoriia. I’m a web developer currently working with WordPress and Astro.
          </h1>

          <p class="hero__text">
            I build websites from design and planning through development, testing, and launch. Most of my recent work includes custom WordPress themes, ACF, Custom Post Types, and Astro projects. I also have experience with React, React Native, TypeScript, PHP, and other front-end technologies.
          </p>

          <div class="hero__actions">
            <a href="#projects" class="button button--primary">
              View Projects
            </a>

            <a
              href={`${base}/ViktoriiaMatviieva_WordPress_Developer.pdf`}
              class="button button--secondary"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              View Resume
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__card">
          <p class="hero__card-label">Core Skills</p>

          <div class="skill-list">
            <span>WordPress</span>
            <span>Custom WordPress Themes</span>
            <span>Elementor</span>
            <span>Advanced Custom Fields</span>
            <span>Custom Post Types</span>
            <span>WP_Query</span>
          
            <span>Astro</span>
            <span>React</span>
            <span>React Native</span>
            <span>Redux</span>
            <span>TypeScript</span>
            <span>JavaScript ES6</span>
            <span>PHP</span>
            <span>HTML5</span>
            <span>CSS3</span>

          
            <span>Responsive Development</span>
            <span>Figma to Code</span>
  
          
            <span>SEO</span>
            <span>Website Performance</span>
            <span>Accessibility</span>
          
            <span>Google Analytics 4</span>
            <span>Google Search Console</span>
          
            <span>Git</span>
          
            <span>AI-Assisted Development</span>
            <span>Cursor AI</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="projects" id="projects">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="section-heading__eyebrow">My Work</p>

          <h2 class="section-heading__title">
            Recent Projects
          </h2>

          <p class="section-heading__text">
            A few websites I have designed and developed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="projects__grid">
         
        
          <!-- HOTLINE APPAREL -->
        
          <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-card__body">
              <div class="project-card__top">
                <div>
                  <p class="project-card__label">Agency Project</p>
                  <h3 class="project-card__title">Hotline Apparel</h3>
                </div>
        
                <a
                  href="https://hotlineapparel.ca"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="project-card__link"
                >
                  Visit Site
                </a>
              </div>
        
              <p class="project-card__role">
                <strong>Role:</strong> Web Developer at SecurIBC
              </p>
        
              <div class="project-card__content">
                <p>
                  <strong>Client Goal:</strong>
                  Replace an outdated website with a modern design that clearly
                  explains custom printing and embroidery services to different types
                  of customers.
                </p>
        
                <p>
                  <strong>Challenge:</strong>
                  The existing website had very little content, and the client was still
                  deciding how the company should be presented online. Existing page
                  URLs also needed to be preserved during the rebuild.
                </p>
        
                <p>
                  <strong>Approach:</strong>
                  I worked directly with the client through several discovery sessions,
                  planned the content and page structure, and created wireframes.
                  Elementor was chosen for its flexible visual layouts and because it
                  allows the client to update page content more easily after launch.
                </p>
        
                <p>
                  <strong>Result:</strong>
                  I rebuilt the website from scratch, created the responsive layouts,
                  optimized the images, and added redirects for old URLs. The finished
                  site has a stronger visual style and presents the company’s services
                  more clearly.
                </p>
              </div>
        
              <div class="project-card__tags">
                <span>Client Discovery</span>
                <span>Requirements Gathering</span>
                <span>Content Planning</span>
                <span>Wireframing</span>
                <span>WordPress</span>
                <span>Elementor</span>
                <span>Figma</span>
                <span>Responsive Design</span>
                <span>Image Optimization</span>
                <span>URL Redirects</span>
                <span>Cross-Browser Testing</span>
              </div>
            </div>
        
            <a
              href="https://hotlineapparel.ca"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="project-card__image-link"
              aria-label="Visit the Hotline Apparel website"
            >
              <img
              src={`${base}/Hotline.webp`}
                alt="Hotline Apparel website preview placeholder"
                class="project-card__image"
                width="800"
                height="1000"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </a>
          </article>
        
          <!-- CARRIER AUTO CENTRE -->
        

<article class="project-card">
  <div class="project-card__body">
    <div class="project-card__top">
      <div>
        <p class="project-card__label">Agency Project</p>
        <h3 class="project-card__title">Carrier Auto Centre</h3>
      </div>

      <a
        href="https://carrierautocentre.com"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="project-card__link"
      >
        Visit Site
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="project-card__role">
      <strong>Role:</strong> Web Developer at SecurIBC
    </p>

    <div class="project-card__content">
      <p>
        <strong>Client Goal:</strong>
        Build a professional automotive website with a strong SEO foundation
        and clear pages for each service the company provides.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Challenge:</strong>
        The homepage design was provided, but the rest of the website still
        needed to be designed and developed. The client also needed a simple
        way to manage a growing number of automotive service pages.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Approach:</strong>
        I developed a fully custom WordPress theme without using a page builder.
        This gave me more control over the HTML structure, performance, and
        technical SEO. I also designed the internal pages and created a Custom
        Post Type for managing services.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Result:</strong>
        The client received a fast, responsive website with consistent service
        pages and a cleaner technical foundation for SEO. New services can be
        added and updated directly through the WordPress.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card__tags">
      <span>WordPress</span>
      <span>Custom Theme</span>
      <span>PHP</span>
      <span>HTML</span>
      <span>CSS</span>
      <span>JavaScript</span>
      <span>Custom Post Types</span>
      <span>SEO</span>
      <span>Performance Optimization</span>
      <span>Responsive Design</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a
    href="https://carrierautocentre.com"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="project-card__image-link"
    aria-label="Visit the Carrier Auto Centre website"
  >
    <img
    src={`${base}/Carrier.webp`}
      alt="Carrier Auto Centre website preview placeholder"
      class="project-card__image"
      width="800"
      height="1000"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </a>
</article>
<!-- GARY HUNTER LAW -->

<article class="project-card">
  <div class="project-card__body">
    <div class="project-card__top">
      <div>
        <p class="project-card__label">Agency Project</p>
        <h3 class="project-card__title">Gary Hunter Law</h3>
      </div>

      <a
        href="https://garyhunterlaw.com/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="project-card__link"
      >
        Visit Site
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="project-card__role">
      <strong>Role:</strong> Web Developer at SecurIBC
    </p>

    <div class="project-card__content">
      <p>
        <strong>Client Goal:</strong>
        Create a professional website that reflects the firm’s legal services and
        allows the team to update the content themselves after launch.
      </p>
    
      <p>
        <strong>Challenge:</strong>
        The law firm had separated from another business, but Google and several
        online directories still treated them as one company. Old business names,
        listings, and website references had to be found and corrected.
      </p>
    
      <p>
        <strong>Approach:</strong>
        I designed and built the website in WordPress using Elementor, giving the
        client an easier way to update pages and content. I also optimized the
        Elementor build for page speed, accessibility, responsive performance, and
        technical SEO.
      </p>
    
      <p>
        I reviewed online business listings, found outdated references, and
        contacted directory owners to update the business name, website, and company
        information.
      </p>
    
      <p>
        <strong>Result:</strong>
        The new website gives the firm a clear and professional online presence.
        Google now recognizes it as a separate business, relevant keyword visibility
        is growing, and the site performs well in search.
      </p>
  
    </div>

    <div class="project-card__performance">
      <p class="project-card__performance-title">
        <strong>Performance:</strong>
        Optimized WordPress and Elementor build with strong Lighthouse results.
      </p>
    
      <a
        href="https://pagespeed.web.dev/analysis/https-garyhunterlaw-com/89ogk1e64b?form_factor=desktop"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="project-card__performance-link"
        aria-label="Open the Gary Hunter Law PageSpeed Insights report"
      >
        <img
        src={`${base}/gary-hunter-law-lighthouse.png`}
          alt="Lighthouse results: 99 Performance, 97 Accessibility, 96 Best Practices, and 92 SEO"
          class="project-card__performance-image"
          width="671"
          height="106"
          loading="lazy"
        />
    
      </a>
    </div>



    <div class="project-card__tags">
      <span>WordPress</span>
      <span>Elementor</span>
      <span>Web Design</span>
      <span>Client Discovery</span>
      <span>Content Planning</span>
      <span>Local SEO</span>
      <span>Technical SEO</span>
      <span>Business Listing Cleanup</span>
      <span>Directory Outreach</span>
      <span>Performance Optimization</span>
      <span>Accessibility</span>
      <span>Core Web Vitals</span>
      <span>Responsive Design</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a
    href="https://garyhunterlaw.com/"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="project-card__image-link"
    aria-label="Visit the Gary Hunter Law website"
  >
    <img
    src={`${base}/Gary-Hunter-Law.webp`}
      alt="Gary Hunter Law website preview placeholder"
      class="project-card__image"
      width="800"
      height="1000"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </a>
</article>

 <!-- IT PRODUCTIONS -->
        
 <article class="project-card">
  <div class="project-card__body">
    <div class="project-card__top">
      <div>
        <p class="project-card__label">Freelance Project</p>
        <h3 class="project-card__title">IT Productions</h3>
      </div>

      <a
        href="https://itproductions.org"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="project-card__link"
      >
        Visit Site
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="project-card__role">
      <strong>Role:</strong> Freelance WordPress Developer
    </p>

    <div class="project-card__content">
      <p>
        <strong>Client Goal:</strong>
        Create a website where a nonprofit theatre company could manage its
        shows, auditions, actors, and team members.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Challenge:</strong>
        The project had a limited nonprofit budget but required several
        connected content types and an admin area that would be simple for the
        client to use.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Approach:</strong>
        I managed the project from the first client meetings through launch
        and developed a custom WordPress theme. I used Custom Post Types, ACF,
        and custom WP_Query logic to connect actors with individual shows.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Result:</strong>
        The client can add and update shows, auditions, actors, and team
        members without editing the website code.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card__tags">
      <span>Client Discovery</span>
      <span>Requirements Gathering</span>
      <span>Content Planning</span>
      <span>WordPress</span>
      <span>Custom Theme</span>
      <span>PHP</span>
      <span>HTML</span>
      <span>CSS</span>
      <span>JavaScript</span>
      <span>Custom Post Types</span>
      <span>ACF</span>
      <span>WP_Query</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a
    href="https://itproductions.org"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="project-card__image-link"
    aria-label="Visit the IT Productions website"
  >
    <img
    src={`${base}/IT-Productions.webp`}
      alt="IT Productions website preview placeholder"
      class="project-card__image"
      width="800"
      height="1000"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </a>
</article>
<!-- 3D MECHANICAL -->

<article class="project-card">
  <div class="project-card__body">
    <div class="project-card__top">
      <div>
        <p class="project-card__label">Ongoing Agency Project</p>
        <h3 class="project-card__title">3D Mechanical</h3>
      </div>

      <a
        href="https://3dmechanical.ca/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="project-card__link"
      >
        Visit Site
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="project-card__role">
      <strong>Role:</strong> Web Developer at SecurIBC
    </p>

    <div class="project-card__content">
      <p>
        <strong>Client Goal:</strong>
        Improve the company’s search visibility and attract larger commercial
        and industrial projects rather than residential enquiries.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Challenge:</strong>
        The original website was very general and did not clearly explain the
        company’s industrial capabilities. The client initially wanted to focus
        only on SEO and was hesitant to change the website structure, content,
        or design.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Approach:</strong>
        I explained why SEO improvements also required clearer content and
        stronger positioning. Working within a limited budget, I reorganized the
        website around industrial services and target industries, removed
        residential messaging, and updated the design to better reflect the
        scale of the company’s work.
      </p>

      <p>
        I used a combination of custom WordPress development and Elementor,
        depending on the needs of each page. The current phase of the project is
        focused on technical SEO, service content, keyword targeting, and
        continued search optimization.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Progress:</strong>
        The website now presents 3D Mechanical as an industrial B2B company and
        is more closely aligned with the type of projects they want. Search
        visibility has improved, and the site is appearing less often for
        residential and small consumer-focused searches.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="project-card__tags">
      <span>WordPress</span>
      <span>Custom Theme</span>
      <span>Elementor</span>
      <span>SEO Strategy</span>
      <span>Technical SEO</span>
      <span>Keyword Targeting</span>
      <span>Content Strategy</span>
      <span>Content Restructuring</span>
      <span>B2B Positioning</span>
      <span>Information Architecture</span>
      <span>Responsive Design</span>
      <span>Ongoing Optimization</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <a
    href="https://3dmechanical.ca/"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    class="project-card__image-link"
    aria-label="Visit the 3D Mechanical website"
  >
    <img
    src={`${base}/3D.webp`}
      alt="3D Mechanical industrial metal fabrication website"
      class="project-card__image"
      width="1200"
      height="2000"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </a>
</article>

        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <p>
        © {currentYear} Viktoriia Matviieva. All rights reserved.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>